Spine concept map
Updated: 2026-06-17
Ref: 37fb262f0
Role: map, not canon

Purpose:
Explain how we use "canon" without getting trapped in exception soup.

Preferred word:
- Use "spine" when possible.
- Spine means shared shape proven by code, guards, and nearest siblings.
- Domain deltas are allowed only after the shared spine is visible.

Vertical links:
- Parent: ../../AGENTS.md
- Child: runtime-package.readme
- Child: pages.readme
- Child: components.readme
- Child: composables.readme
- Child: console.readme
- Child: firestore-entity.readme

Horizontal links:
- family-console-entity.readme
- family-public-index.readme
- family-public-detail.readme
- family-menu.readme
- family-tenant-global.readme

Before editing:
1. Name the family.
2. Name the nearest sibling.
3. Name the shared shape.
4. Name the accepted delta.
5. Patch the smallest useful slice.

Stop signals:
- A tiny behavior needs many unrelated files.
- A helper name hides confusion instead of naming a real seam.
- A new layer duplicates an existing core seam.
- A local project app starts owning shared domain behavior.

Useful current spines:
- Console: `core`, `index`, `overview`, `identity`, `team`, `operations`.
- Firestore entity: root entity folder plus `fetch`, `mutations`, `seo`, `utils`.
- Runtime package: `src/module.ts`, `src/config/module/*`, `src/runtime/*`.
- Domain UI: `X/Cards`, `X/Collection`, `X/Create`, `X/Edit`, `Console/X/*`.

Open questions:
- Whether "canon" remains the right word. "Spine" is clearer and less ceremonial.
